### Power BI – Transition to an App-Based Delivery Model

While Microsoft recommends using Power BI Apps as the preferred method for distributing reports to business users, moving directly to this model is not necessarily the right approach for our organisation at this stage. As we transition from an on-premises Power BI environment to the online service, users are already adapting to changes in how reports are accessed, managed and shared. Introducing an App-based delivery model immediately would add another layer of change, requiring additional user education, communication and support. Users need to understand not only how to access Power BI Apps, but also why we are introducing them and what benefits they provide.

The proposed approach is to initially provide controlled access to reports through their respective Production workspaces, with appropriate security and governance in place. Over time, as users become more familiar with Power BI Online and our governance processes mature, we can progressively introduce Power BI Apps where they provide clear business value. Not every report necessarily needs to be delivered through an App, and some reports may continue to be accessed directly through workspaces where appropriate. This phased approach allows us to align with Microsoft's recommended practices without introducing unnecessary complexity or disruption to the business.
